iation ma1 mep 1 direction inward\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 remote-mep 2\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 test-profile test1 two-way-delay-measurement peer-ip 1.1.1.1 test-id 1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Huawei command combines several functions into one line (test-id, MEP association, peer IP, and implied delay measurement configuration), while Juniper requires separate statements to achieve the same functionality. The interval and count parameters are distributed across different Juniper commands (interval in CC, count implied by loss-threshold).\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 remote-mep 2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 test-profile test1 two-way-delay-measurement peer-ip 1.1.1.1 test-id 1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the given Huawei CFM test configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check interval 1s loss-threshold 20\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 mep 1 direction inward\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 remote-mep 2\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 test-profile test1 two-way-delay-measurement peer-ip 1.1.1.1 test-id 1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Huawei command combines several functions into one line (test-id, MEP association, peer IP, and implied delay measurement configuration), while Juniper requires separate statements to achieve the same functionality. The interval and count parameters are distributed across different Juniper commands (interval in CC, count implied by loss-threshold).\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 test-profile test1 two-way-delay-measurement peer-ip 1.1.1.1 test-id 1'}]]": 1,
    "['delay-measure two-way send test-id [parameter1] interval [parameter2] count [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check transmission interval 1s', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper JUNOS command for the HUAWEI CFM delay measurement configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check transmission interval 1s\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check transmission loss-measurement two-way\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 mep 1 loss-measurement two-way packets 20\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper implements CFM (802.1ag) slightly differently than HUAWEI. While HUAWEI combines delay measurement and loss measurement in a single command, Juniper separates these functions. The equivalent functionality is achieved through these three commands that configure two-way loss measurement with 1-second intervals and 20 packets.\\n\\nThe \"delay-measure\" functionality in HUAWEI is most closely matched by Juniper\\'s two-way loss measurement feature, as Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct \"delay-measure\" command in its CFM implementation.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check transmission interval 1s'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check transmission loss-measurement two-way', 'parent_c